{
 "dur": 74.3,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "Thousands of cars burning gasoline,",
    "in a tube under a river.",
    "How does the Holland Tunnel breathe?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 7.03,
   "chunks": [
    "Opened in 1927,",
    "it runs over a mile and a half",
    "under the Hudson,",
    "New Jersey to Manhattan."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 14.27,
   "chunks": [
    "The killer was carbon monoxide.",
    "Tests at Yale and the Bureau of Mines",
    "found just four parts in ten thousand",
    "was dangerous."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 22.8,
   "chunks": [
    "Chief engineer Clifford Holland",
    "died in 1924, before it opened.",
    "Ole Singstad designed the ventilation,",
    "and finished it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 31.66,
   "chunks": [
    "His answer:",
    "split the tube into three layers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 35.33,
   "chunks": [
    "Fans blow fresh air",
    "into a duct under the roadway.",
    "It rises through slots along the curb."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 41.03,
   "chunks": [
    "Dirty air is pulled up",
    "through vents in the ceiling,",
    "into an exhaust duct above, and out."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 46.54,
   "chunks": [
    "Four ventilation buildings,",
    "two on land and two out in the river,",
    "hold eighty-four fans.",
    "Forty-two blow in. Forty-two pull out."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 55.54,
   "chunks": [
    "Together, they can replace",
    "all the air in the tunnel",
    "every ninety seconds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 60.18,
   "chunks": [
    "It was the world's first",
    "mechanically ventilated tunnel.",
    "Today it's a National Historic Landmark."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 66.74,
   "chunks": [
    "What should we take apart next?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v12",
   "t": 69.04,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "how the Holland Tunnel breathes."
   ]
  }
 ]
}